.TH MLH-SETTINGS-BACKEND 1 "November 2026" "mlh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mlh-settings-backend \- read and update mlh settings as JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mlh-settings-backend
.RB { snapshot | apply }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snapshot
prints a JSON document containing sections, fields, and actions.
Secret values are never included in the output.
.B apply
reads a schema version 1 JSON request from standard input, applies its
changes and actions, and prints the updated snapshot.
The graphical and terminal settings interfaces use this command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mlh-settings-gtk (1),
.BR mlh-settings-tui (1)
